From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: the folder view's IShellFolderView, IViewObject and IFolderView2 view properties (3694)

shell32: the folder view's IShellFolderView, IViewObject and IFolderView2 view properties

IShellFolderView (Rearrange, GetArrangeParam, ArrangeGrid, AddObject,
UpdateObject, RefreshObject, SetItemPos, Select, GetItemSpacing, SetPoints,
SetClipboard, GetDragPoint, GetDropPoint, IsDropOnSource, IsBkDropTarget,
SetCallback, SetAutomationObject) work on the list as documented; SetObjectCount
stays E_NOTIMPL (documented so since Vista); GetSelectedCount no longer crashes
when nothing is selected.

IViewObject draws the list, freezes and unfreezes its picture, and sends
OnViewChange notices to the advise sink it now holds a reference on.

IFolderView2 caches view properties (shown in the column), takes tile
property lists, the text of an empty view, the group subset count, and
answers IsMoveInSameFolder.

The XP-only IShellFolder2::EnumSearches no longer logs a FIXME.
